<Page current="about" title="About — It's Not Easy Being Bjorn"><div class="inner">
<p>
    Meet Bjorn. He's a decent fellow. A little scruffy,
    perpetually weary, and rather good at fixing things.
  </p>

  <p>
    Bjorn likes to help. He builds things, solves problems,
    notices trouble before it arrives, and generally tries
    to do right by the people around him. Unfortunately,
    the people around him have other ideas.
  </p>

  <p>
    To his friends and neighbours, Bjorn is alternately
    indispensable and insufferable. His competence is admired
    until it becomes inconvenient. His generosity is
    appreciated until it becomes expected. His honesty is
    welcome until someone doesn't like what he has to say.
  </p>

  <p>
    And when things inevitably go wrong, well, there's
    usually Bjorn to blame.
  </p>

  <p>
    Bjorn isn't perfect. He's stubborn, sometimes too
    trusting, and rather slow to recognize when he's being
    taken advantage of. He still believes that reasonable
    people ought to be able to reason with one another.
    It's a belief that gets tested rather frequently.
  </p>

  <p>
    <em>It's Not Easy Being Bjorn</em> is a black-and-white
    comic about human nature, misplaced responsibility,
    moral absurdity, and the curious ways people turn those
    who help them into the villains of their stories.
  </p>

  <p>As Bjorn has learned:</p>

  <blockquote>
    <p>
      Those who make you responsible for everything
      will eventually blame you for something.
    </p>
  </blockquote>

<p>
  The concepts and scripts are my own work. The images are generated
  with ChatGPT because I’m not a very good artist. Bjorn deserves
  better than my stick figures; he’s dealing with enough already.
</p>
</div>
</Page>
